{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_01UnxhKsRYnZ7aL7at2xtvTB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Let me provide a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## US-003 Implementation Complete\n\nI've successfully implemented the in-memory event storage with CRUD operations. Here's what was delivered:\n\n### Implementation Summary\n\n**src/events/store.rs** (443 lines):\n\n1. **EventStore Trait** - Defines the interface with methods:\n   - `create()` - Create new events\n   - `read()` - Retrieve events by ID\n   - `update()` - Update existing events\n   - `delete()` - Remove events by ID\n   - `list()` - Get all events sorted by start time\n   - `query_by_date_range()` - Filter events by date range\n   - `query_by_category()` - Filter events by category\n   - `query_by_date_range_and_category()` - Combined filtering\n\n2. **InMemoryEventStore Implementation**:\n   - HashMap-based storage for O(1) lookups\n   - Proper error handling with `EventStoreError` enum\n   - All query methods return sorted results\n\n3. **Error Handling**:\n   - `NotFound` - Event doesn't exist\n   - `AlreadyExists` - Duplicate event ID\n   - `InvalidDateRange` - Start date after end date\n\n4. **Comprehensive Unit Tests** (18 tests covering):\n   - Create operations (including duplicates)\n   - Read operations (existing and non-existent)\n   - Update operations (existing and non-existent)\n   - Delete operations (existing and non-existent)\n   - List functionality with sorting\n   - Date range queries with validation\n   - Category filtering\n   - Combined date range and category queries\n   - Empty store edge cases\n\n### Acceptance Criteria Status\n\n- ✅ EventStore trait defined with CRUD methods\n- ✅ InMemoryEventStore implementation working\n- ✅ Can create and retrieve events\n- ✅ Can update existing events\n- ✅ Can delete events\n- ✅ Can query events by date range\n- ✅ Unit tests for all operations\n- ⚠️  car